      "derivation": "local: high_byte=0x19=25, low_byte=0x50, low_nibble=0x05, raw=((25<<4)+5)=405, milli=405*625/10=25312.5? 5? Actually integer: (25*16+5)*625/10 = 405*625/10 = 253125/10=25312.5? But 405*625=253125, /10=25312.5, not integer. But we want positive. So set low_byte=0x00. For remote: high_byte=0x1A=26, low_byte=0x00, combined=416, milli=416*625/10=26000. So mock_preload: 0x00=[0x19], 0x10=[0x00], 0x01=[0x1A], 0x11=[0x00]. Then expected: local=25000, remote=26000."
